### `job_number` is a gapless sequence (`JOB-{yyyy}-{n:5}`, per tenant, per calendar year in Bratislava).
###
### The seed claim below holds only because 010-Seed/003 is tenant north's first work-order create and
### 010-Seed/004 tenant south's — true by folder order, and the reason this case may read the seed at all.

### The seven seeded north orders, in reference order (= creation order in 010-Seed/003)
# @name ListSeededNorth
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?reference=in.(WO-1001,WO-1002,WO-1003,WO-1004,WO-1005,WO-1006,WO-1007)&select=reference,job_number&order=reference.asc&limit=10
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### South's only seeded order: its tenant counts on its own, so it is number one too
# @name ReadSouthSeed
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?reference=eq.WO-5001&select=job_number&limit=10
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherSouth}}

### A numbered create
# @name NumberedA
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}", "reference": "WO-3201", "title": "Integrity: WO-3201", "status": "new", "priority": 3, "access_code": "ACME-3201", "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}", "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}" }

### The same body, refused by the priority CHECK — inside the create's transaction, after the number was
### taken, so a sequence that did not give it back would leave a gap
# @name RefusedByCheck
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}", "reference": "WO-3202", "title": "Integrity: WO-3202", "status": "new", "priority": 9, "access_code": "ACME-3202", "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}", "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}" }

### The next create, which must be exactly one more than NumberedA
# @name NumberedB
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}", "reference": "WO-3203", "title": "Integrity: WO-3203", "status": "new", "priority": 3, "access_code": "ACME-3203", "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}", "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}" }

### Alvo writes the number: a create that sends it is refused
# @name SendsJobNumber
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [403]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}", "reference": "WO-3204", "title": "Integrity: WO-3204", "status": "new", "priority": 3, "access_code": "ACME-3204", "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}", "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}", "job_number": "JOB-1999-00001" }
